WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.530
Finding a few fallen lashes every morning? Don't worry, that's completely normal!

2
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:12.005
Every lash goes through three stages: growth, transition, then rest and shedding.

3
00:00:12.005 --> 00:00:17.288
The growth stage lasts about four to six weeks, and the lash gets longer every day.

4
00:00:17.288 --> 00:00:21.646
Growing lashes are short and fine, so they get light extensions.

5
00:00:21.646 --> 00:00:26.678
The transition stage only lasts two to three weeks, and the lash stops growing.

6
00:00:26.678 --> 00:00:31.827
Don't pull or pluck your lashes now, because the new one will grow back more slowly.

7
00:00:31.827 --> 00:00:37.348
The resting stage lasts a few months, then the lash sheds and a new one takes its place.

8
00:00:37.348 --> 00:00:43.123
Because every lash is at a different stage, losing two to five lashes a day is normal.

9
00:00:43.123 --> 00:00:49.282
An extension is bonded to a natural lash, so when that lash sheds, the extension goes with it.

10
00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:53.249
That's not a fault. Just book a refill every two to three weeks.

11
00:00:53.249 --> 00:01:02.335
In short: a lash grows, goes through transition, rests and sheds, and extensions simply fall out with your natural lashes.

12
